B.u0. {"problem": "The change request asks for a note saying why the owner agreed, but nothing stores a reason. confirm_element has no param for the reason, no effect writes it, and Element has no field for it. Setting records_decision: true does not create a why-note. On decide and approve_commit the same flag also carries no reason field. The request is not delivered.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element (records_decision), object Element", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u1. {"problem": "The diff sets confirm_element to status: proposed, although the request gave no instruction to demote it. Every other action and every transition cell that refers to it is confirmed. The domain would be deployed with an unconfirmed element on the main confirmation path. The source was also swapped from the ADR record to an interview line, L34, with no quote, so the new grounding cannot be checked.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element (status, source)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u2. {"problem": "Other actions also bring an Element to confirmed: confirm_all_proposed, which calls confirm_element for every proposed element, and confirm_wording_fix. Neither gets records_decision, so confirmations made through them keep no note. The request says \"each confirmation\", so these paths are inconsistent with the change.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions confirm_all_proposed and confirm_wording_fix", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u3. {"problem": "Behaviour changes for confirm_element: it now records a decision, as decide, approve_commit and deploy do. But its transition cells, the scenario a-confirmed-element-is-not-unknown-again, and the glossary entries for element and approval do not reflect a recorded decision or a reason. The scenario calls confirm_element with no reason or params, so it would not exercise the new note.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, scenarios a-confirmed-element-is-not-unknown-again, transitions Element, glossary", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
B.u4. {"problem": "The authoring declaration changes the behaviour of an action in its interface, but the version is still 17. The composition pins interface 1 and is not updated.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version; toprope-self.composition.yaml, members.authoring", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u5. {"problem": "The change request asks for a note saying why the owner agreed, but nothing captures a reason. confirm_element has no params, and Element has no property to hold a note. The only change is the flag `records_decision: true`. Even if that flag logs a decision, the owner has no way to supply the reason, so the stated goal is not met.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.confirm_element (params) and objects.Element (properties)", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u6. {"problem": "confirm_element is now `status: proposed` with a new interview source (L34) that has no quote. A declaration that is still unconfirmed by a person is being deployed, and it is the very action that gates confirmation. The authoring domain's own rule says only a person confirms elements. The action's status is not a confirmed owner decision, and the change cites no evidence that the owner agreed.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.confirm_element (source, status)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u7. {"problem": "Other actions also bring an Element to confirmed, but they record no decision or reason. confirm_wording_fix has no `records_decision` and no `requires: human`, and an agent may take it on the owner's behalf. confirm_all_proposed has `requires: human` but no `records_decision`. After the change, only confirm_element keeps a note, so the aim of a note on each confirmation fails. The rule only-a-person-element-confirmed, which says every confirming action requires a person, is also already untrue for confirm_wording_fix.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.confirm_wording_fix, actions.confirm_all_proposed, rules.only-a-person-element-confirmed", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
B.u8. {"problem": "The behaviour of confirm_element changes, but the authoring `version` stays at 17. The interface the composition pins (authoring interface: 1) is not revisited. The scenario a-confirmed-element-is-not-unknown-again calls confirm_element with no reason, so it may fail or no longer reflect real use if a reason is now needed.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml version; scenarios.a-confirmed-element-is-not-unknown-again; toprope-self.composition.yaml members.authoring", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
B.u9. {"problem": "The request asks for a note saying why the owner agreed, but the change only adds the flag `records_decision: true` to confirm_element. There is no param for a reason, no Element property to hold a note, and no effect that stores one. Nothing in the declaration captures the owner's reasoning, so the requested behaviour is not delivered. The flag only mirrors the one on approve_commit, decide and deploy, which also take no reason.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element (and object Element, which has no note property)", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u10. {"problem": "The diff sets confirm_element's status to `proposed`, but the file as it stands after the change shows `status: confirmed`. The change record and the final file disagree. If `proposed` is what was intended, the action is no longer owner-confirmed and may not deploy as a confirmed element. If `confirmed` is what is there, it rests on interview line L34 with no quote, and the request gives no reason or owner agreement for the change.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element: status and source", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u11. {"problem": "The source for confirm_element was swapped from the ADR-0037 record to interview L34, with no quote. Nothing in the change request shows that this interview line is where the owner agreed to recording a decision on confirmations. The provenance of the rule is unverified.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element source", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
B.u12. {"problem": "Other paths still bring an Element to confirmed and ignore the new behaviour. confirm_all_proposed calls the same kernel confirm_element with 'all' and has `requires: human` but no `records_decision`. confirm_wording_fix also confirms with the same call, and has neither `requires: human` nor `records_decision`. 'Each confirmation' therefore does not get a note, and the three confirmation paths are now inconsistent with each other.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions confirm_all_proposed and confirm_wording_fix", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
B.u13. {"problem": "The rule says every action that brings an Element to confirmed requires a person (confirm_element). confirm_wording_fix has no `requires: human` and moves an Element from proposed to confirmed in the transitions matrix. Its description says an agent may do it. The rule's reason text was written for a single action and is already false. This change makes confirmation semantics matter more, since decisions are now recorded for one path but not for the other.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, rules.only-a-person-element-confirmed vs confirm_wording_fix", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
B.u14. {"problem": "A behaviour change to confirm_element was made without bumping the domain version (still 17). The composition pins authoring at interface 1, so consumers cannot tell that the action's recording behaviour changed.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members.authoring", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u15. {"problem": "The change request asks for a note saying why the owner agreed, but confirm_element only gains records_decision: true. It has no param for the reason, and Element has no field to hold one. The flag records who decided, as it does on decide, approve_commit and deploy. It does not record a reason. record_confirmation also sets nothing. So no why-note is kept.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.confirm_element, objects.Element", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u16. {"problem": "Confirmations that bypass confirm_element carry no note. confirm_wording_fix and confirm_all_proposed make the same confirm_element kernel call and move Elements to confirmed, but neither has records_decision or a reason. 'Each confirmation' is therefore not covered.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.confirm_wording_fix and actions.confirm_all_proposed", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
B.u17. {"problem": "The diff also changes confirm_element's status from confirmed to proposed and swaps its source from a record to an interview line (L34) with no quote. The request does not ask for this. The action that confirms every other element is now itself unconfirmed in the declaration. That likely blocks the change from being approved, or leaves the domain with an unconfirmed element. The interview L34 citation is unverified and may not exist.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.confirm_element source/status", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u18. {"problem": "The behaviour of a deployed action changes, since confirmations are now recorded as decisions, but the domain version stays at 17. The change is not versioned.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u19. {"problem": "The rule only-a-person-element-confirmed says confirm_element is the only action that brings an Element to confirmed. confirm_wording_fix and confirm_all_proposed also do so, and neither requires a person (confirm_wording_fix has no requires: human). The rule's reason is stale. This gap exists in the files as they stand and is not new to this change, but it matters more once confirmation is meant to be a recorded human decision.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, rules.only-a-person-element-confirmed", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
B.u20. {"problem": "The change request asks for a note saying why the owner agreed, but the change only sets `records_decision: true`. confirm_element has no param (such as a reason) to carry the owner's why, and the call to the kernel (`paths`, `approver`) does not pass one. The note may therefore be empty or not stored. The same flag on `decide`, `approve_commit` and `deploy` likewise has no reason param.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element (params and effects)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u21. {"problem": "Other actions also confirm elements through the same `confirm_element` kernel call but do not record a decision or a why. confirm_all_proposed confirms every proposed element in bulk, and confirm_wording_fix confirms without a person. 'Each confirmation' is therefore not covered, and the ledger will be inconsistent depending on which action confirmed the element.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions confirm_all_proposed and confirm_wording_fix", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u22. {"problem": "The diff sets confirm_element to `status: proposed` with a new interview source (L34), but the file after the change shows `status: confirmed`. The submitted change and the resulting file disagree. If it really is proposed, an unconfirmed action is being deployed in a domain where every other element is confirmed, and the Element transition cell `proposed.confirm_element` still cites the old interview L6 source. The new source (interview L34) has no quote, so it does not show the owner agreed to this change.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action confirm_element (source/status)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u23. {"problem": "The scenario a-confirmed-element-is-not-unknown-again calls confirm_element as owner with no params. Once the action records a decision with a reason, this step may be denied or may record an empty note. The scenario was not updated for the new behaviour and does not test the note.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, scenario a-confirmed-element-is-not-unknown-again", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u24. {"problem": "This is a behaviour change to the deployed authoring declaration (confirming now records a decision), but `version` is still 17 in the file after the change. The composition still pins interface 1, and the change is not reflected for the Delivery handoff or for consumers.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}

